comments.body:
> Are you expecting `rpool/zvols` to be a volume?

As of https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/issues/15351#issuecomment-1749486202 I would say that he didn't, the output for rpool/zvols likely is to show non-default properties on the parent datasets that'll be inherited into the zvol one.

@reporter: maybe you could try to determine the on-disk differences between fresh installs with both settings of `zvol_use_blk_mq`? Something like diffs between the filesystems in the VM images, to detect broken files... which could provide some clues to what is going wrong...
